LIBPKGAUDIT(3)

# NAME

libpkgaudit - backend-neutral package integrity audit library

# SYNOPSIS

```
#include <libpkgaudit/libpkgaudit.h>
```

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgaudit* compares an immutable package-object inventory with typed
filesystem observations and returns a structured report.

The library does not open a package database.  A consumer constructs
*pkgaudit::inventory* from its own authority and supplies a
*pkgaudit::filesystem_backend*.  The library has no dependency on
libpkgstate or libpkgcore.

# MODEL

An inventory contains package identifiers and canonical root-relative
objects.  Durable object identity is either directory or non-directory.
Shared ownership is retained.

An audit request explicitly selects packages and checks.  Filesystem
requests carry stable identifiers.  Backends may return responses in
any order, but must return exactly one matching response for every
request.

A report contains integrity findings, neutral ownership relations, and
audit failures.  The report is complete only when the failure stream is
empty.

# FINDINGS

Object-state checks may report missing objects and durable class
mismatches.  Symlink checks may report dangling links, loops, and target
escape from the selected root.

Ownership checks classify a resolved target as owned by the source
package, owned by another package, or unowned.  Severity is not part of
the library result.

# FILESYSTEM BACKEND

*make_posix_filesystem_backend*(3) opens one target root and performs
descriptor-relative observations with lstat semantics.  Absolute
symlink targets are interpreted inside that root.  Resolution is
bounded and target reads are checked for concurrent change.

# ERRORS

Construction and request errors throw subclasses of
*pkgaudit::audit_error*.  Per-object probe failures and backend protocol
violations are returned in the report rather than silently ignored.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgchk*(1)

